From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:09:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply default metadata values sent to /addgames for existing
 games

MetaDataList::loadFromXML skips every value equal to its default. That
is fine when a gamelist is parsed into new FileData, but /addgames
reuses the existing FileData, so values that reset a field are dropped:
posting <favorite>false</favorite> or <lastplayed>0</lastplayed> for a
game that is a favorite, or has been played, does nothing.

Only skip a default value when the field is not set yet. Empty values are
still skipped, so partial entries do not clear other fields.
Startup parsing is unchanged: new FileData has no fields set, and
gamelist recovery files never contain default values.
---
 es-app/src/MetaData.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-app/src/MetaData.cpp b/es-app/src/MetaData.cpp
index c5cb3478..1adbf1b8 100644
--- a/es-app/src/MetaData.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/MetaData.cpp
@@ -210,7 +210,9 @@ void MetaDataList::loadFromXML(MetaDataListType type, pugi::xml_node& node, Syst
 		if (mdd.id == MetaDataId::GenreIds)
 			continue;
 
-		if (value == mdd.defaultValue)
+		// Skip default values, unless they replace a value that is already set
+		// (e.g. favorite=false or lastplayed=0 sent to /addgames for an existing game)
+		if (value == mdd.defaultValue && (value.empty() || mMap.find(mdd.id) == mMap.cend()))
 			continue;
 
 		if (mdd.type == MD_BOOL)
